WEBVTT

00:00:00.610 --> 00:00:03.370
<i>I'm Nishimiya Ryo, 15 years old,
high school first-year.</i>

00:00:03.790 --> 00:00:05.510
<i>When I got back from the training camp,</i>

00:00:05.510 --> 00:00:09.700
<i>my father said something shocking
upon returning home from London.</i>

00:00:12.030 --> 00:00:13.860
Dad! When did you get back?

00:00:13.860 --> 00:00:16.360
Ryo, I have some good news.

00:00:16.360 --> 00:00:18.700
Things are finally on track at work,

00:00:18.700 --> 00:00:21.980
so we'll be able to all live in London
together as a family starting in January!

00:00:23.340 --> 00:00:25.020
That's awesome!

00:00:25.020 --> 00:00:27.280
It's been so long. I wonder
how much has changed.

00:00:27.280 --> 00:00:30.470
I'm sure it hasn't changed
that much in ten years.

00:00:31.010 --> 00:00:34.480
Okay, time to check out the latest
Vivienne Westwood designs then.

00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:37.760
We can finally all live together as a family.

00:00:38.210 --> 00:00:40.110
I'm sorry it's taken so long.

00:00:40.110 --> 00:00:41.390
Isn't this great?

00:00:41.390 --> 00:00:43.930
You've always said how
living in Japan doesn't agree with you

00:00:43.930 --> 00:00:47.140
and that being in London was easier.

00:00:47.140 --> 00:00:48.810
Th-That's...

00:00:47.790 --> 00:00:50.700
Is that what you were saying, Ryo?

00:00:50.700 --> 00:00:54.520
Then I guess you're going to apply
at Cambridge or Oxford for university?

00:02:27.450 --> 00:02:31.330
Dream Galaxy, 
Compassion Planet

00:02:36.620 --> 00:02:37.700
Hey!

00:02:38.760 --> 00:02:40.050
Hey, Kouta.

00:02:40.050 --> 00:02:42.220
It's really starting to feel like
the school festival around here.

00:02:42.220 --> 00:02:44.150
We only have a month left. Scary.

00:02:44.150 --> 00:02:45.350
Time flies.

00:02:45.350 --> 00:02:46.550
Flies?

00:02:46.550 --> 00:02:48.110
You have to include "like an arrow".

00:02:48.650 --> 00:02:50.130
Only if we were in the archery club.

00:02:50.540 --> 00:02:53.610
Wouldn't it be a bit obsessive
to say that there?

00:02:53.610 --> 00:02:54.690
We say it all the time.

00:02:55.140 --> 00:02:56.110
Seriously?

00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:08.720
There's only one month
left until the school festival.

00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:11.210
Cast / Pomrin Duchy Nobleman Koural - Kouta / 
/ Cinnaamoll Empire Prince Sei - President / Cinnaamoll Empire Knight Candidate Yuucisus - Yuu / 
/ Kikiira Kingdom Prince Riyon - Ryo / Kikiira Kingdom Knight Candidate Shuun - Shunsuke / 
/ Script - Yuu (And Ryo) / Backgrounds - Shunsuke, President, Kouta / 
/ Props - Ryo, Kouta / Costumes - Yuu, Kouta / Music - Kouta

00:03:08.720 --> 00:03:11.210
We have to really power
through and do our best!

00:03:11.210 --> 00:03:12.960
That's all well and good,

00:03:12.960 --> 00:03:15.760
but aren't you taking on too much, Kouta?

00:03:15.760 --> 00:03:17.320
I'll be fine.

00:03:17.320 --> 00:03:21.220
I don't have club activities or student council
or assistant things like the rest of you.

00:03:21.220 --> 00:03:24.570
I'm the one who doesn't have anything,
so I want to work even harder!

00:03:24.570 --> 00:03:26.810
You know, I'm in the go
straight home club, too.

00:03:27.180 --> 00:03:30.280
You have to make food for Yuri-chan, 
who's studying for entrance exams though.

00:03:30.280 --> 00:03:32.260
Besides, this was my idea to begin with.

00:03:32.260 --> 00:03:34.020
I should be the one to do the most work.

00:03:34.330 --> 00:03:36.680
But are you sure you're okay
with the music and all that?

00:03:37.020 --> 00:03:39.360
I'm sure. I have some ideas.

00:03:39.360 --> 00:03:40.570
You're really enthusiastic.

00:03:40.570 --> 00:03:41.980
Of course I am.

00:03:41.980 --> 00:03:44.120
It's the first time I've found
something that I really want to do.

00:03:44.120 --> 00:03:45.660
I'm going to give it my all!

00:03:47.530 --> 00:03:48.770
What's wrong, Nishimiya?

00:03:49.140 --> 00:03:50.220
Did something happen?

00:03:50.640 --> 00:03:52.160
Nothing at all.

00:03:53.330 --> 00:03:54.130
Okay.

00:03:56.510 --> 00:03:59.990
Let's all do our best for the school festival!

00:03:59.990 --> 00:04:01.540
We're going to sparkle!

00:04:01.540 --> 00:04:02.860
Yeah.

00:04:04.810 --> 00:04:05.730
Excuse me,

00:04:05.730 --> 00:04:08.930
we were hoping to start
the council meeting, President.

00:04:08.930 --> 00:04:10.100
My apologies.

00:04:10.100 --> 00:04:11.270
Sorry about that.

00:04:11.530 --> 00:04:13.220
We'll get out of here now.

00:04:15.600 --> 00:04:18.770
We can use this classroom
as our work space from now on.

00:04:18.770 --> 00:04:21.570
Quickly getting us a free classroom to use...

00:04:21.570 --> 00:04:24.130
Nicely done, President! Using that influence!

00:04:24.460 --> 00:04:28.300
I just went through the normal
procedures. I didn't use my influence.

00:04:28.300 --> 00:04:30.010
I know that.

00:04:30.010 --> 00:04:32.530
You're always so serious, Seiichirou-san.

00:04:32.530 --> 00:04:34.260
But it's still a huge help,

00:04:34.260 --> 00:04:36.840
especially since we've always been
gathering in the student council room.

00:04:36.840 --> 00:04:39.090
We didn't think about needing a work space.

00:04:39.710 --> 00:04:43.020
Well, now that our new base
has been established,

00:04:43.020 --> 00:04:46.840
once again, let's all do our best
for the school festival!

00:04:47.030 --> 00:04:48.230
Yeah, I'm sorry.

00:04:49.310 --> 00:04:52.860
I have the student council going on,
so I can't help out today.

00:04:52.860 --> 00:04:55.670
Oh, that's right.
There was a meeting mentioned.

00:04:55.670 --> 00:04:56.850
I have soccer.

00:04:56.850 --> 00:05:00.020
Captain told me I'd live to
regret it if I skipped today.

00:05:00.020 --> 00:05:02.110
You definitely shouldn't
be skipping on practice.

00:05:02.110 --> 00:05:05.020
I also have my assistant job to do.

00:05:05.020 --> 00:05:05.950
Okay, then.

00:05:06.330 --> 00:05:07.750
I'll be free tomorrow.

00:05:08.570 --> 00:05:09.370
So will I.

00:05:09.370 --> 00:05:10.110
Me, too.

00:05:10.110 --> 00:05:12.750
Okay, so it's just you and me today then, Yuu.

00:05:12.750 --> 00:05:13.700
Sorry!

00:05:13.700 --> 00:05:18.530
Yuri's practice exam grade came
back yesterday and I promised her

00:05:18.530 --> 00:05:22.350
I would make her cake for dessert
at dinner since she got an A.

00:05:22.350 --> 00:05:24.450
Wow, that's great for Yuri-chan!

00:05:24.450 --> 00:05:26.470
You better head home and make it then.

00:05:26.470 --> 00:05:29.480
I'll totally help you tomorrow though. Sorry.

00:05:29.480 --> 00:05:31.240
It's fine, don't worry about it.

00:05:31.560 --> 00:05:34.680
I did say I'd do my best
since everyone else is busy.

00:05:37.740 --> 00:05:42.260
<i>Seems like everyone is fulfilled by
all the various things they're doing.</i>

00:05:44.560 --> 00:05:47.280
<i>All right, I'm going to do my best, too!</i>

00:05:50.910 --> 00:05:54.910
Continuing on, about the applications
for additional budgets for club activities...

00:05:54.910 --> 00:05:58.770
Right, we've had a large number of
applications tied to the school festival.

00:05:58.770 --> 00:06:01.450
Most of the clubs have sent one in.

00:06:02.050 --> 00:06:06.010
If I go through them all, the preparations
for the school festival will be stalled.

00:06:07.190 --> 00:06:09.220
Vice President, will you go
through half of them?

00:06:10.140 --> 00:06:13.190
Please consult with me if there
are any really difficult cases.

00:06:13.920 --> 00:06:17.010
Anything other than that, please go over
it with accounting at your discretion.

00:06:17.010 --> 00:06:18.520
Are you sure about that?!

00:06:18.520 --> 00:06:21.740
It's not a good idea to make people
waiting on budgets wait much longer, is it?

00:06:22.840 --> 00:06:24.700
You've really changed, President.

00:06:24.700 --> 00:06:25.500
Have I?

00:06:25.760 --> 00:06:28.740
You used to say that you would
do everything yourself before!

00:06:30.370 --> 00:06:32.830
If I push it too much,
I'll just get scolded again.

00:06:33.690 --> 00:06:34.620
By them.

00:06:36.040 --> 00:06:38.730
Now then, with the entrance exam
group of third-years moving on,

00:06:38.730 --> 00:06:42.810
it's time to start making a new team
to aim for the winter championships.

00:06:42.810 --> 00:06:45.160
Well, I'm one of the ones
in the entrance exam group.

00:06:45.160 --> 00:06:47.440
That's why I'm thinking
of nominating a new captain

00:06:47.440 --> 00:06:49.380
and just being a normal team member.

00:06:50.840 --> 00:06:52.590
After speaking with the other third-years,

00:06:52.590 --> 00:06:55.800
it was unanimously decided that
the new captain will be Yoshino.

00:06:57.110 --> 00:06:57.910
We're counting on you.

00:06:57.910 --> 00:06:59.590
There's no way I can do this!

00:06:59.590 --> 00:07:01.250
We want it to be you, too.

00:07:01.250 --> 00:07:02.320
So do we.

00:07:02.600 --> 00:07:05.680
Tomo-san, you kept this all a secret from me.

00:07:07.230 --> 00:07:12.010
A captain has to make plans like this
or else he can't lead his team to victory.

00:07:12.010 --> 00:07:14.570
You've learned something,
haven't you, new captain?

00:07:14.570 --> 00:07:17.330
I really can't do this, I'm not cut out to be—

00:07:17.600 --> 00:07:18.700
Why are you running away?

00:07:20.630 --> 00:07:22.960
Hey, at least just think it over.

00:07:22.960 --> 00:07:24.920
It really was a unanimous decision.

00:07:25.370 --> 00:07:28.290
Everyone said they want to
fight with you at the center.

00:07:30.090 --> 00:07:32.310
All right, I'll do it.

00:07:32.840 --> 00:07:34.900
Really? You'll do it?

00:07:34.020 --> 00:07:35.500
Yeah!

00:07:35.500 --> 00:07:38.780
Well then, new captain, let's
get you started with your first task.

00:07:38.780 --> 00:07:39.600
Okay.

00:07:39.950 --> 00:07:41.390
As you know,

00:07:41.390 --> 00:07:44.540
the first task of any new captain of
Hijirikawa High School's soccer team

00:07:44.540 --> 00:07:46.860
is one lap of ground dribbling—

00:07:47.400 --> 00:07:48.790
wearing only your underwear!

00:07:49.600 --> 00:07:53.570
And the new regular team member's
first task is to catch the new captain!

00:07:50.220 --> 00:07:51.820
Hey, stop it!

00:07:54.930 --> 00:07:56.580
Don't let him get away!

00:07:58.850 --> 00:08:00.920
Let's see, next is...

00:08:00.920 --> 00:08:02.040
Onii-chan,

00:08:02.610 --> 00:08:04.840
if you're going to make me
a cake, put this on it.

00:08:06.070 --> 00:08:07.800
I already know what you like.

00:08:09.590 --> 00:08:10.920
Aren't I awesome?

00:08:12.030 --> 00:08:14.590
Are you sure you're okay to make a cake though?

00:08:14.910 --> 00:08:17.310
Didn't you say you had something
to do for the school festival?

00:08:17.310 --> 00:08:18.430
Seriously?!

00:08:18.430 --> 00:08:19.470
Wh-What?

00:08:19.990 --> 00:08:24.100
You're actually worried
about me, I'm so happy!

00:08:24.600 --> 00:08:25.990
That's so gross!

00:08:26.310 --> 00:08:27.720
That attack won't work anymore.

00:08:27.720 --> 00:08:31.150
Gross, gross, gross, gross,
gross, gross, gross, gross!

00:08:29.950 --> 00:08:31.150
Doesn't work at all!

00:08:38.330 --> 00:08:40.330
<b>Explore the History of London</b>

00:08:42.300 --> 00:08:43.220
Nishimiya-kun.

00:08:44.410 --> 00:08:46.230
What's the matter? Are you okay?

00:08:46.230 --> 00:08:47.630
Yeah, I'm fine.

00:08:55.850 --> 00:08:57.640
Ah, welcome back, Ryo-chan!

00:08:57.640 --> 00:08:59.240
Welcome home, sugar.

00:08:59.240 --> 00:08:59.970
Welcome back.

00:08:59.970 --> 00:09:00.910
What's all this?

00:09:00.910 --> 00:09:04.260
Since your father is already
renting a home in London

00:09:04.260 --> 00:09:06.830
he told us to send over whatever items we can.

00:09:06.830 --> 00:09:09.860
You go and grab some things you can send, too.

00:09:09.860 --> 00:09:11.420
I'll pack them in my luggage.

00:09:11.850 --> 00:09:14.770
It's best to do these things a bit at a time.

00:09:14.770 --> 00:09:16.150
Go on, go get some things.

00:09:16.630 --> 00:09:17.430
Ryo.

00:09:22.590 --> 00:09:23.390
Okay.

00:09:33.240 --> 00:09:34.920
It's not stable.

00:09:36.090 --> 00:09:37.460
I'll hold it down.

00:09:38.230 --> 00:09:40.730
Huh? Do we have anymore of these buttons?

00:09:40.730 --> 00:09:43.130
Yeah, I'm pretty sure I have some.

00:09:43.130 --> 00:09:43.930
Here you go.

00:09:44.270 --> 00:09:46.460
Aren't you overdoing it a bit, Kouta?

00:09:46.460 --> 00:09:49.530
Well, I dragged everyone
into something I want to do,

00:09:49.910 --> 00:09:51.980
so I have to work harder.

00:09:51.980 --> 00:09:55.080
We don't feel like we've been dragged into this.

00:09:55.080 --> 00:09:58.300
Yeah, I know everyone has said so,

00:09:58.300 --> 00:10:00.030
but I want to work hard.

00:10:00.030 --> 00:10:01.630
Just don't overdo it.

00:10:01.630 --> 00:10:02.820
I'll be fine.

00:10:02.820 --> 00:10:04.490
I have more free time than you guys do.

00:10:06.470 --> 00:10:09.230
Oh, Ryo, if there's anything you
need for the props and whatnot,

00:10:09.230 --> 00:10:11.840
just let me know and I'll go get it.

00:10:11.840 --> 00:10:12.960
Yeah, sure.

00:10:15.870 --> 00:10:16.970
See ya!

00:10:16.970 --> 00:10:18.270
See you tomorrow.

00:10:25.330 --> 00:10:27.390
Well then, bye, Senpai.

00:10:27.390 --> 00:10:28.190
Yeah.

00:10:34.010 --> 00:10:34.810
Nishimiya.

00:10:36.830 --> 00:10:38.550
Something is going on, isn't it?

00:10:40.290 --> 00:10:42.270
You can talk to me if you want.

00:10:48.580 --> 00:10:50.150
So that's what's going on.

00:10:50.150 --> 00:10:53.430
Suddenly being told we're going to be
in London in January was too much.

00:10:54.270 --> 00:10:56.670
So, what would you like to do?

00:10:56.920 --> 00:11:00.940
I don't know, but my feelings
don't really matter.

00:11:01.530 --> 00:11:02.300
Why not?

00:11:03.470 --> 00:11:06.450
My dad is always deciding things on his own,

00:11:06.450 --> 00:11:09.770
but my mom and my sisters trust him.

00:11:09.770 --> 00:11:13.270
Being the youngest, there's
nothing I can really say to my dad.

00:11:13.630 --> 00:11:17.920
But I'm sure your father wants
to know what you think.

00:11:17.920 --> 00:11:19.540
How do you know?

00:11:19.860 --> 00:11:21.450
Because I'm the same way.

00:11:22.380 --> 00:11:23.500
Senpai...

00:11:23.500 --> 00:11:27.090
If you really talk to your dad,
I'm sure that he'll listen.

00:11:27.830 --> 00:11:31.490
So be sure to face him and
tell him how you feel.

00:11:33.450 --> 00:11:34.230
Nishimiya.

00:11:34.660 --> 00:11:37.330
Then please come to my house next time.

00:11:38.170 --> 00:11:41.530
I might be able to talk to my dad
better if you're there.

00:11:43.970 --> 00:11:45.030
Can you?

00:11:46.090 --> 00:11:47.110
Okay, then.

00:11:48.330 --> 00:11:50.600
If it'll help you, then I'll go.

00:11:51.320 --> 00:11:52.600
Thank you so much!

00:11:52.600 --> 00:11:53.630
But,

00:11:54.400 --> 00:11:57.810
you have to be the one to talk to him.

00:11:57.810 --> 00:11:58.610
Okay.

00:12:03.880 --> 00:12:05.050
Hey there, Ryo-chan.

00:12:05.910 --> 00:12:08.110
What do you want, Mizuno-san?

00:12:08.110 --> 00:12:09.540
Here, this is your portion.

00:12:10.430 --> 00:12:11.660
What is it?

00:12:11.660 --> 00:12:15.280
Well, I made too much cake
for my sister yesterday—

00:12:15.280 --> 00:12:17.630
Oh, it has peaches on it, I hope that's okay.

00:12:17.630 --> 00:12:18.880
It's fine.

00:12:20.080 --> 00:12:23.600
By the way, what's your favorite fruit?

00:12:23.600 --> 00:12:25.260
It's melon.

00:12:25.260 --> 00:12:26.560
Is that so?

00:12:26.960 --> 00:12:28.160
One other thing, Ryo.

00:12:28.160 --> 00:12:28.960
Yes?

00:12:28.960 --> 00:12:31.720
When we were at the training
camp the other day,

00:12:31.720 --> 00:12:33.500
we ate the same food
and spent the night together,

00:12:33.500 --> 00:12:36.070
which means we're friends now.

00:12:36.400 --> 00:12:39.320
I don' t really like you how said that,

00:12:39.320 --> 00:12:40.650
but I guess that's true.

00:12:40.930 --> 00:12:46.160
So, I want the people I'm friends
with to be as happy as possible,

00:12:46.160 --> 00:12:49.780
which means I will do whatever
I can to make that happen.

00:12:50.990 --> 00:12:52.200
Which means!

00:12:52.810 --> 00:12:56.280
If there's anything that's
bothering you, you can tell me.

00:12:59.710 --> 00:13:01.990
But, if there isn't anything, that's fine.

00:13:01.990 --> 00:13:04.220
If there isn't, yep.

00:13:07.930 --> 00:13:11.590
<i>Even Mizuno-san has noticed
that I'm anxious about something.</i>

00:13:13.850 --> 00:13:15.940
Hey, Ryo.

00:13:15.940 --> 00:13:17.320
Y-Yes?

00:13:17.320 --> 00:13:18.240
You know.

00:13:18.240 --> 00:13:18.950
Huh?

00:13:18.950 --> 00:13:21.850
If there's anything going on, 
I'll listen if you need to talk.

00:13:22.800 --> 00:13:25.010
I may not be the best person but...

00:13:25.600 --> 00:13:26.500
Right...

00:13:30.880 --> 00:13:31.960
Yoshino-san.

00:13:32.380 --> 00:13:33.180
What?

00:13:33.580 --> 00:13:35.400
Are you going to check that out?

00:13:36.620 --> 00:13:39.920
I-I'm going to use this for soccer reference.

00:13:40.170 --> 00:13:41.740
Yeah, that's right.

00:13:42.860 --> 00:13:45.040
<i>Everyone is so nice...</i>

00:13:43.670 --> 00:13:46.420
<b>Introduction to Baseball</b>

00:13:46.840 --> 00:13:51.760
I'm sorry, we have to have this overnighter
because I'm behind on things.

00:13:52.040 --> 00:13:55.660
That's why I said you were
taking on too much to begin with.

00:13:55.980 --> 00:13:58.860
I'm actually happy we're staying the night.

00:14:00.050 --> 00:14:02.710
The truth is, tomorrow is my birthday.

00:14:05.080 --> 00:14:08.140
How unfriendly of you, Ryo-chan.

00:14:08.140 --> 00:14:11.550
If you'd told us beforehand,
we could've prepared something.

00:14:12.070 --> 00:14:13.830
Yeah, that's right.

00:14:14.720 --> 00:14:17.230
It's fine. I don't really like a big fuss.

00:14:17.230 --> 00:14:22.230
My family tends to go all out,
so if my birthday fell on a Sunday,

00:14:22.230 --> 00:14:25.510
they would throw me a party
that would last all day.

00:14:25.510 --> 00:14:29.220
<b>Incidentally, there was a pre-birthday evening
party and a post-birthday evening party last year.</b>

00:14:28.680 --> 00:14:30.960
So please don't worry about it.

00:14:30.960 --> 00:14:34.490
Let's just focus on getting
the work done that we're behind on.

00:14:34.490 --> 00:14:36.930
Well, if you say so.

00:14:41.480 --> 00:14:43.530
It may be our second time
here, but it's still huge.

00:14:43.530 --> 00:14:44.900
Rock-paper-scissors for it?

00:14:44.900 --> 00:14:46.730
Okay, I'm not gonna lose this time!

00:14:47.600 --> 00:14:49.360
Sure, let's do it.

00:14:49.600 --> 00:14:52.340
Starting with rock. Rock,
paper, scissors, shoot!

00:14:55.660 --> 00:14:58.500
I thought I'd heard
rock-paper-scissors last time, too,

00:14:58.500 --> 00:15:00.350
what were you guys doing out there?

00:15:00.350 --> 00:15:02.660
Having a manly competition.

00:15:02.660 --> 00:15:04.600
It's pretty childish.

00:15:04.760 --> 00:15:07.700
You're the one who suggested it!

00:15:08.960 --> 00:15:13.040
If you don't stop throwing
rock when you get excited,

00:15:13.040 --> 00:15:15.270
you're always going to be the
one ringing the doorbell.

00:15:15.270 --> 00:15:17.570
Ryo, you're not supposed to tell him.

00:15:17.960 --> 00:15:20.270
What is Seiichirou doing?

00:15:20.620 --> 00:15:24.260
He said that he and his friends are putting
on a performance at the school festival.

00:15:24.260 --> 00:15:26.190
But he's an entrance exam student.

00:15:26.190 --> 00:15:27.740
What's the big deal?

00:15:27.740 --> 00:15:31.720
Now he's even more fired up
that he can't fail the exam.

00:15:31.720 --> 00:15:35.080
In fact, neither his practice test grades
nor his school grades have gone down.

00:15:35.390 --> 00:15:39.580
And what's more, he's made friends
he wants to spend time with.

00:15:44.250 --> 00:15:45.590
You can use this room.

00:15:46.360 --> 00:15:47.170
It's huge!

00:15:47.170 --> 00:15:48.940
This will be perfect.

00:15:48.940 --> 00:15:50.650
It's like an inn.

00:15:50.650 --> 00:15:54.230
When my family gets together,
we have our celebrations here.

00:15:55.340 --> 00:15:57.260
Well then, let's get started!

00:15:57.870 --> 00:16:00.580
Already? Can't we take a break?

00:16:00.580 --> 00:16:03.190
Sure, but I'm going to get started.

00:16:04.330 --> 00:16:05.480
All right, let's do it!

00:16:05.480 --> 00:16:09.120
Shunsuke and I are in charge of the stage sets,
so we'll help with other things, too.

00:16:09.120 --> 00:16:09.920
Okay.

00:16:11.930 --> 00:16:13.770
Mizuno-san and I will come up with ideas

00:16:13.770 --> 00:16:16.670
for the development of the last
part of the script then.

00:16:16.670 --> 00:16:18.890
Guess I have to then, okay.

00:16:43.580 --> 00:16:46.350
I think we can call it a day, don't you?

00:16:47.570 --> 00:16:48.790
You're right.

00:16:48.790 --> 00:16:50.740
Shall we take turns starting
with those who are free

00:16:50.740 --> 00:16:52.620
taking baths and then going to bed?

00:16:52.960 --> 00:16:55.860
Oh, but I'm going to be a bit longer.

00:16:55.860 --> 00:16:57.150
Me, too, I think.

00:16:57.150 --> 00:16:59.490
Oh, um, me too, me too.

00:16:59.490 --> 00:17:02.580
I can't exactly go before a guest,

00:17:03.150 --> 00:17:04.880
so why don't you go first, Nishimiya?

00:17:05.840 --> 00:17:07.210
S-Sure.

00:17:07.610 --> 00:17:08.630
I'll show you where it is.

00:17:08.630 --> 00:17:09.620
Okay.

00:17:21.200 --> 00:17:22.930
I wonder if they've already gone to sleep...

00:17:28.460 --> 00:17:30.410
Happy Birthday!

00:17:31.450 --> 00:17:34.890
We already knew that today was your birthday.

00:17:35.280 --> 00:17:38.690
We factored that into the training camp, too.

00:17:38.690 --> 00:17:40.860
Sorry, I let them do it.

00:17:42.990 --> 00:17:46.870
It's my handmade birthday
cake using lots of melon.

00:17:47.150 --> 00:17:50.160
So this is why you asked me
what my favorite fruit was?

00:17:50.160 --> 00:17:51.840
Okay, one, two, three...

00:17:52.130 --> 00:17:55.610
Happy birthday to you,

00:17:55.610 --> 00:17:58.720
happy birthday to you,

00:17:58.940 --> 00:18:03.090
happy birthday dear Ryo.

00:18:03.090 --> 00:18:07.940
Happy birthday to you!

00:18:15.710 --> 00:18:17.300
Congrats!

00:18:19.480 --> 00:18:20.480
Jeez,

00:18:20.910 --> 00:18:23.620
didn't I say I didn't need anything like this?

00:18:24.020 --> 00:18:26.710
We need to be working on making
progress on our work, don't we?

00:18:27.110 --> 00:18:30.830
Besides, the birthday person
is supposed to wear those hats.

00:18:30.830 --> 00:18:33.130
What are you doing, standing out more?

00:18:33.920 --> 00:18:37.020
What are you all smiling so happily for?

00:18:37.020 --> 00:18:39.270
Does someone else's birthday
really make you that...

00:18:43.870 --> 00:18:44.840
Thank you.

00:18:45.570 --> 00:18:51.290
Kouta-kun, Yuu-kun,
Shunsuke-kun, Seiichirou-san.

00:18:55.850 --> 00:18:57.270
I'm really happy.

00:19:01.910 --> 00:19:03.010
So good.

00:19:03.010 --> 00:19:04.330
Seriously good.

00:19:05.050 --> 00:19:06.320
What do you think, Ryo-chan?

00:19:06.320 --> 00:19:08.520
It's amazingly delicious.

00:19:08.520 --> 00:19:10.420
Thank you for the honest praise.

00:19:11.060 --> 00:19:13.000
Do you have a special recipe?

00:19:13.000 --> 00:19:15.530
I basically wing it.

00:19:15.530 --> 00:19:17.840
It tastes different each time you take a bite.

00:19:17.840 --> 00:19:19.370
But it's good each time, right?

00:19:19.370 --> 00:19:21.370
Make one for my birthday, too.

00:19:21.370 --> 00:19:22.530
Okay.

00:19:22.530 --> 00:19:24.210
Then what's your least favorite fruit?

00:19:24.210 --> 00:19:26.880
Why are you asking what fruit I don't like?

00:19:29.950 --> 00:19:32.040
There's something I want
to talk to you all about.

00:19:32.830 --> 00:19:33.730
Nishimiya.

00:19:34.320 --> 00:19:38.380
My father said that we would be
living in London starting in January.

00:19:38.810 --> 00:19:40.060
I've been agonizing over it this whole time.

00:19:40.060 --> 00:19:41.220
Really?

00:19:41.220 --> 00:19:42.820
So that's what it was.

00:19:43.360 --> 00:19:45.450
You seemed pretty off lately.

00:19:45.890 --> 00:19:47.780
So you both noticed, too.

00:19:48.810 --> 00:19:50.660
I'm the only one who didn't notice?

00:19:50.660 --> 00:19:53.540
Thank you for telling us.
We'll do our best to help you.

00:19:53.870 --> 00:19:54.670
Yeah.

00:19:55.140 --> 00:19:56.270
Me, too!

00:19:56.270 --> 00:19:59.880
Thank you. But you're all so important
to me and I want to be friends with you

00:19:59.880 --> 00:20:03.950
rather than being an underclassman
who makes you worry,

00:20:03.950 --> 00:20:07.190
so I think I want to figure
this out on my own for now.

00:20:08.760 --> 00:20:12.070
That's also why I want you to please
forget about what I asked you, Senpai.

00:20:12.950 --> 00:20:14.450
Okay, got it.

00:20:14.450 --> 00:20:15.480
What are you talking about?

00:20:15.840 --> 00:20:17.230
That's a secret.

00:20:17.230 --> 00:20:19.360
Hey, it's not fair to keep secrets!

00:20:19.360 --> 00:20:21.070
Oh, come on, now.

00:20:21.840 --> 00:20:26.240
Anyway, when I have reached a conclusion,
I will be sure to let you all know.

00:20:26.640 --> 00:20:27.610
Okay, then.

00:20:27.950 --> 00:20:31.000
But if anything is bothering you, let us know.

00:20:33.830 --> 00:20:34.630
I will!

00:22:09.410 --> 00:22:10.210
Hase.

00:22:10.840 --> 00:22:11.990
Hey, Hase!

00:22:12.830 --> 00:22:13.750
You okay?

00:22:14.570 --> 00:22:17.480
Oh, Tsucchi, Macchi. What's up?

00:22:17.480 --> 00:22:19.280
Don't "what's up" us.

00:22:19.280 --> 00:22:21.900
You've been working way too hard lately.

00:22:22.220 --> 00:22:24.850
You're always nodding off in class, too.

00:22:24.850 --> 00:22:27.550
How much work are you putting
in here after school?

00:22:28.700 --> 00:22:31.300
Thanks for worrying about me guys,

00:22:31.750 --> 00:22:33.850
but if I don't work hard
we won't make it in time.

00:22:34.720 --> 00:22:36.450
Then we'll help you.

00:22:36.450 --> 00:22:37.750
No, you don't need to.

00:22:38.160 --> 00:22:40.460
I'm pretty good at these things y'know.

00:22:41.030 --> 00:22:42.660
Both the light music club and the

00:22:42.660 --> 00:22:44.650
baseball team are participating
in the school festival, right?

00:22:44.650 --> 00:22:48.050
I'd feel bad if your projects 
didn't go well because of me.

00:22:51.700 --> 00:22:53.700
We got dumped again.

00:23:00.880 --> 00:23:04.720
<i>Besides, this is something
I have to work on myself.</i>

00:23:15.110 --> 00:23:17.870
<i>I'm going to do my best to shine, too.</i>

00:23:34.970 --> 00:23:40.380
Next Episode

00:23:36.500 --> 00:23:38.650
Next time, <i>"In The Dark"</i>.
